What the signals borrow
-----------------------

The method is assembled from published work and the provenance is recorded in
`msrc/signals.py` and the README. Those citations are to papers and techniques,
not to redistributed code: no source from SelfCheckGPT, Semantic Entropy,
LLM-Check, SAPLMA or any other project is vendored here.

Vendored source
---------------

One third-party file is redistributed, and it is the only one:

  references/m4c_evaluator.py

  The answer processor and accuracy evaluator used for TextVQA. It carries
  Facebook's original copyright header and its own note that the processor was
  copied from `facebookresearch/mmf` at commit c46b3b3391275b4181567db80943473a89ab98ab.
  It is vendored for one reason: indicator 2.2 is reported with the official
  TextVQA soft accuracy, and computing that must not depend on a network fetch at
  evaluation time. A short provenance note was added above the copyright header;
  nothing below it was edited.

  This repository's Apache-2.0 licence does not extend to that file. Its terms are
  the upstream project's terms, which are not restated here because they were not
  verified when the file was added -- check `facebookresearch/mmf` before relying
  on it. Nothing else in this repository is derived from it, and the framework
  runs without it: TextVQA soft accuracy is the only thing that needs it.
